// std/norm (spec/std.md 60, decision 0476). Declaration file. Unicode
// normalization of golang.org/x/text/unicode/norm: the four forms of UAX
// #15 (NFC, NFD, NFKC, NFKD) on Str, so two spellings of the same text
// (`é` as one rune or `e` and a combining accent) compare equal after
// `normalize(s, Form.Nfc)`. Unicode 15.0.0.

/// A normalization form.
enum Form {
  /// Canonical decomposition, then canonical composition (the usual form for
  /// storing and comparing text).
  Nfc
  /// Canonical decomposition.
  Nfd
  /// Compatibility decomposition, then canonical composition.
  Nfkc
  /// Compatibility decomposition.
  Nfkd
} derive Display

/// The Unicode version of the tables (`15.0.0`).
fn unicode_version() -> Str

/// s in the form f (Form.String). ASCII text is returned as it is.
fn normalize(s: Str, f: Form) -> Str
/// Whether s is already in the form f (Form.IsNormalString).
fn is_normalized(s: Str, f: Form) -> Bool
